# Kill the recurring 4xx from clients that auto-request legacy icon paths.
# The site ships an SVG favicon (linked in <head>), but browsers, bots, and
# link-preview crawlers still probe these fixed paths — each a 404 otherwise.
# A 302 to the real icon is a 3xx, not a 4xx, so analytics stay clean. (Every
# other unknown path is a real 404 now — site/404.html — so these three matter.)
/favicon.ico                       /favicon.svg   302
/apple-touch-icon.png              /favicon.svg   302
/apple-touch-icon-precomposed.png  /favicon.svg   302
